    },
    {
      "target": "u2",
      "focus": [],
      "change": "KEEP",
      "reason": "`G2` supports both the matching-type requirement and the recovery clause: for the pan task `P5:28` takes pot 1 (wrong noun) and then repeats the same placement at `P5:36` and `P5:43` until the step limit, while for the pot task `P7` switches from pan 1 to pot 2 at `P7:16`, cools it at `P7:18`, and completes at `P7:20`. The `different target` branch is not directly demonstrated (P5's failure was object type, not target), but it is offered only as an alternative to the type-matching switch, and no supplied evidence shows it is harmful. Keep the whole Update.",
      "to": null
    },
    {
      "target": "u3",
      "focus": [
        "S"
      ],
      "change": "Keep the direction (search closed containers and avoid re-checking), but make the trigger implementable under the Actor's information access and broaden coverage: ground \"already inspected\" in what the Actor can observe (e.g., a location visible in the last two observation/action pairs), treat every distinct container and surface listed in the scene — including not-yet-reached ones such as diningtable and further cabinets/drawers — as a candidate, and forbid cycling among the same few locations.",
      "reason": "Direction is supported: `G1`'s `P2` opens fridge (`P2:5`), cabinets (`P2:12`, `P2:30`) and microwave (`P2:19`) but never drawers or shelves and never finds bread, returning to already-seen spots (`P2:16`, `P2:48`) to the step limit, while `P3:4` and `P4:41` show countertop and diningtable surfaces reveal the needed bread directly and `P4` completes at `P4:47`. Historical `M2` (`S1_R02/diff`) shows the same coverage/anti-revisit wording only partly worked: the candidate in `S1_R02/Q8` cycled among fridge, countertop, cabinets, shelves and drawer (`S1_R02/Q8:21`) and never reached the initially listed diningtable, ending at `S1_R02/Q8:50`; `M1` likewise records re-checking empty shelves at `S1_R01/Q7:15`. Because the protocol exposes only the last two observation/action pairs, `locations already shown to be empty` is not fully actionable, so the scope change grounds the anti-revisit trigger in observable recent history, enumerates the candidate containers/surfaces, and forbids cycling. Unverified: broader coverage may add steps when the target is already reachable, and `M2`'s mixed results mean it is not proven to prevent step-limit failure. `c3` is revised to match.",
      "to": {
        "patch": "--- a/SKILL.md\n+++ b/SKILL.md\n@@\n-- When the required object is not visible on surfaces reached so far, search closed containers by opening drawers and cabinets (and the fridge/microwave) and check shelves, moving to unvisited containers rather than re-checking locations already shown to be empty.\n-- Countertops and diningtables reveal their contents directly when reached, so visit unvisited surfaces before returning to already-seen ones.\n+- When the required object is not visible at the current location, keep searching the scene's remaining candidate locations: open closed containers (drawers, cabinets, fridge, microwave) and inspect shelves and open surfaces you have not yet reached, rather than re-checking places you have already inspected.\n+- Treat every distinct container and surface listed in the scene, including ones you have not reached yet (e.g., diningtable and additional cabinets or drawers), as a candidate, and do not cycle among the same few locations.\n+- Countertops and diningtables reveal their contents directly when reached, so reaching a new location is informative; judge whether a place was already inspected only from what you can observe, such as a location visible in the last two observation/action pairs, and otherwise move on to a different candidate.\n"
      }
    },
